---
import Pipeline from "./Pipeline.astro";
import AskKick from "./AskKick.astro";
import { run, scheduleLog } from "../../lib/first-run";
import { bounds, story } from "../../lib/coverage";
import { pipeline, spell, toPlay } from "../../lib/cases";

const sources = [
  ["pages", "Count the matches listed on the pages Kick saved"],
  ["log", "Count the lines in Kick's fetch log"],
  ["rule", "The membership list and the competition's format"],
];
const bar = (n: number) => `${(n / story.scheduled) * 100}%`;
const chain = [
  [story.scheduled, "scheduled, by the rule", ""],
  [story.finals, "finished", `${toPlay} still to be played`],
  [story.afterRepair, "with a score on a saved page", "1 final with no score"],
  [story.counted, "read into Kick's table", `${story.afterRepair - story.counted} on the page that never arrived`],
] as const;
---

<section id="case-dunmore">
  <h2>Case 1. Dunmore: a count needs an expected set</h2>
  <Pipeline small lit="scrape" note="This case happens at Scrape" />

  <p class="cv-callout">Dunmore athletics, 5:44: “You've got our men at six conference games. We've played thirteen.” Riley's table had no way to say thirteen.</p>

  <h3 class="cv-beat"><span class="sr-only">Case 1, </span>Look</h3>
  <p>Besides the table, Kick kept a log of the {run.total} pages it asked for. Of those, {pipeline.boxes} were box scores from Alder Ridge. These are the other {spell(pipeline.asked)}.</p>
  <table class="cv-log">
    <caption>Kick's fetch log, schedule pages</caption>
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">School</th><th scope="col">Result</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>{scheduleLog.map((l) => <tr class:list={{ "is-gap": l.result !== "saved" }}><th scope="row">{l.name}</th><td>{l.result}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
  </table>
  <p>The gap is one line of the log, and the summary never mentions it. So ask Kick.</p>
  <AskKick />

  <h4 class="cv-try">Build the denominator</h4>
  <p>Kick's evidence names the missing page. It cannot say how many matches are missing, because nothing in the run says how many there should be. The competition can.</p>
  <div class="cv-check" data-once="scheduled">
    <div class="cv-line" data-q data-type="select" data-answer="rule" data-why="The membership list and the format. Both exist before the run and apart from it, so a silent school stays in the count." data-wrong={JSON.stringify({ pages: "A school whose page never arrived lists nothing, so it drops out of its own count.", log: "The log counts pages asked for, and only the pages Kick thought to ask for. It holds no matches." })}>
      <label><span>Where can the number of matches come from, before the run?</span>
        <select data-save="q-source"><option value="">Choose</option>{sources.map(([k, t]) => <option value={k}>{t}</option>)}</select>
      </label>
      <p class="cv-fb" role="status"></p>
    </div>
    <div data-q data-type="number" data-answer={story.scheduled} data-why={`${story.scheduled}. ${spell(story.schools, true)} hosts, each with ${spell(story.schools - 1)} visitors: ${story.schools} × ${story.schools - 1}. Nobody has to fetch anything to know it.`}>
      <label for="cv-scheduled">Each of the {spell(story.schools)} schools hosts every other school once. How many conference matches does the season hold?</label>
      <input id="cv-scheduled" inputmode="numeric" autocomplete="off" data-save="q-scheduled" />
      <p class="cv-fb" role="status"></p>
    </div>
    <p class="cv-once">One attempt at both.</p>
    <button type="button" data-submit>Check both</button>
    <p class="cv-fb" role="status" data-need></p>
    <div class="cv-reveal"><p>Of the {story.scheduled}, {spell(toPlay)} are still to be played on Friday.</p></div>
  </div>

  <h3 class="cv-beat"><span class="sr-only">Case 1, </span>Name it</h3>
  <p>Kick never wrote an expected set, so its coverage could not be worked out: {story.counted} found, against nothing. Its log could name the silent page because the log was a list of pages. For matches it had no list at all.</p>
  <p>Survey statisticians call the list of units you set out to hear from the <strong>sampling frame</strong>, and a unit on it that did not answer <strong>unit nonresponse</strong>. Dunmore's page is unit nonresponse.</p>

  <h3 class="cv-beat"><span class="sr-only">Case 1, </span>What Touchline does</h3>
  <p>Its expected rows come from a membership list kept by season, apart from any run, and its totals from the competition's format. Counting what the collected pages list is a weaker third source, complete only as far as the pages are.</p>

  <h3 class="cv-beat"><span class="sr-only">Case 1, </span>Your claim</h3>
  <div class="cv-check" data-once="claim-count">
    <div data-q data-type="range" data-answer={`${story.counted},${story.finals}`} data-why={`${story.counted} of ${story.finals}. Kick's message said ${story.counted}. The denominator is what should exist by now: ${story.scheduled} scheduled, less ${spell(toPlay)} still to play. Not ${story.scheduled}, because unplayed matches cannot be missing, and not ${story.counted}, because a count of what arrived cannot show what did not.`}>
      <p class="cv-qlabel">Write the caption Kick's table needed. Kick's 4:52 message said how many it found.</p>
      <p class="cv-row cv-fillin">
        <span>Built from</span>
        <input inputmode="numeric" autocomplete="off" aria-label="Matches in the table" data-save="claim-count" />
        <span>of</span>
        <input inputmode="numeric" autocomplete="off" aria-label="Finished conference matches" data-save="claim-total" />
        <span>finished conference matches.</span>
      </p>
      <p class="cv-fb" role="status"></p>
    </div>
    <p class="cv-once">One attempt.</p>
    <button type="button" data-submit>Check my caption, and build the chain</button>
    <p class="cv-fb" role="status" data-need></p>
    <div class="cv-reveal">
      <div class="cv-chain" role="img" aria-label={chain.map(([n, what, lost]) => `${n} ${what}${lost ? `, minus ${lost}` : ""}`).join(". ")}>
        {chain.map(([n, what, lost]) => <div>{lost && <p class="cv-drop">minus {lost}</p>}<span class="cv-track"><span style={`width:${bar(n)}`}></span></span><p><b>{n}</b> {what}</p></div>)}
      </div>
      <p>Riley could have known every line of this at 4:52. Now a reader knows the table is short. Which rows to distrust is the next case.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="cv-further">Go further, on a separate page: <a href="../01-collection-field-work/?from=case-dunmore#statistics">Statistics of the gap</a>, where an expected set comes from and what survey statisticians call each kind of gap.</p>
  <p class="cv-next">One page cost {spell(bounds.unseen)} matches. Case 2 asks how far that one page reaches.</p>
</section>
